## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
Issue #104 requires opt-in runtime memory diagnostics for wasm32-wasi programs, with useful source-aware reports and no generic-trap-only fallback.

### Decisions Made
- Use Clang UBSan instrumentation with fatal handlers supplied as WebAssembly imports because the browsercc sysroot has no compatible compiler-rt UBSan archive.
- Validate every non-WASI import after linking so --allow-undefined cannot conceal ordinary unresolved user symbols.
- Pair UBSan with libc++ debug hardening so vector::operator[] and other container preconditions emit descriptive assertion failures.
- Keep the mode disabled unless explicitly requested by the compile payload.

### Trade-offs
- This provides documented UBSan and hardened-library coverage, not ASan-style heap use-after-free detection; ASan is unsupported for the current WASI target.

